From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:39:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Flush the DPI FIFO at frame end on CHV too

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream until tested. The bit is documented for
BXT/GLK only; whether CHV has it is unknown.

Commit f90e8c36c886 ("drm/i915/dsi: fix bxt split screen and color
issue") fixed a picture that appeared split or shifted with the color
components cycled by setting BXT_DEFEATURE_DPI_FIFO_CTR in
MIPI_EOT_DISABLE: per bspec, with the bit set, vblank start is
signalled only when the complete frame has been transferred and the
DPI FIFO is flushed at the end of each frame.

A GPD Win 1 (Cherry Trail, 720x1280 DSI, video mode, non-burst with
sync events) shows the same failure: under load the picture
intermittently ends up shifted (by a line-sized amount, or a few pixels
with the colors rotated, i.e. a byte offset that is not a multiple of
3 in RGB888) and stays so until the next modeset or until it recovers
by itself. Each time, MIPI_INTR_STAT has DPI_FIFO_UNDERRUN latched
while the pipe itself reports no FIFO underrun, and all DSI registers
are unchanged.

Set the bit on CHV in video mode as well, so that an underrun corrupts
at most one frame.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 877eab7..dee674a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -1376,6 +1376,13 @@ static void intel_dsi_prepare(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 		tmp |= BXT_DPHY_DEFEATURE_EN;
 		if (!is_cmd_mode(intel_dsi))
 			tmp |= BXT_DEFEATURE_DPI_FIFO_CTR;
+	} else if (display->platform.cherryview && !is_cmd_mode(intel_dsi)) {
+		/*
+		 * EXPERIMENT: flush the DPI FIFO at the end of each frame as on
+		 * BXT, so that a DPI FIFO underrun cannot leave the pixel stream
+		 * misaligned for the following frames.
+		 */
+		tmp |= BXT_DEFEATURE_DPI_FIFO_CTR;
 	}
 
 	for_each_dsi_port(port, intel_dsi->ports) {
-- 
